</div>
<p><span class="Command">Stitch</span> <span lang="EN-GB">will be successful only if you make correct selection. This means that you must select both sides of the gap in such a way so the two selections to be separated (see picture 2.) After applying the command, two holes remain in both sides of the crack. Select these holes and call</span> <u><span lang="EN-GB"><a href="fill.htm">Fill</a></span></u> <span lang="EN-GB">command with the proper parameter. This way the whole crack will be filled.</span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB">Cracks and splits in meshes can come out because of missing data while scanning or decimating during merge.</span></p>
<p class="Use"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Use</b></span> <span class="Command">Stitch</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command to cover with triangles such areas.</span></p>
